cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software/analysis, please cite the associated manuscript."
title: "Jujubogenin does not preferentially engage the GABA_A benzodiazepine site: an in silico study of a candidate allosteric cavity at the alpha1/gamma2 interface"
abstract: "Purely computational (docking + molecular dynamics + MM-GBSA + in-silico alanine scan) study of jujubogenin binding to the human alpha1beta2gamma2 GABA_A receptor. The benzodiazepine site is not preferentially engaged; an exploratory search identifies a membrane-proximal cavity at the alpha1/gamma2 interface that is stable over 24.8 ns of explicit-solvent MD."
